<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="/markets">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/industrial-iot">Industrial &amp; IoT</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">Power Modules</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Industrial &amp; IoT products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/pcba-box-build"><span class="abbr">PB</span><span class="label">PCBA &amp; Box Build</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/iot-device-assembly"><span class="abbr">ID</span><span class="label">IoT Device Assembly</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/rfid-asset-tracking"><span class="abbr">RT</span><span class="label">RFID Asset Tracking</span></a><a class="s active" href="/markets/industrial-iot/power-modules"><span class="abbr">PM</span><span class="label">Power Modules</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the product does and where it runs and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Industrial &amp; IoT &middot; Power Modules</div><h1 class="mk-h1">Power modules for industrial energy and drives</h1><p class="mk-lede">Hana assembles the power module &mdash; not the inverter, charger or drive it is specified into. Most of the work sits in the thermal path between the die and the cooling the equipment builder has designed around it: multi-die layouts on DBC ceramic, controlled die attach, heavy-current interconnect and encapsulation to the module&rsquo;s specification.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-power-modules" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="height:420px;border-radius:var(--radius-card);border:1px solid var(--line);"><img src="/images/photos/mk-automotive-power-modules-placement.webp" alt="IGBT power module assembly" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;"/></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-power-modules" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">IGBT, SiC and intelligent power modules for motor control run on the same die-attach and bonding lines as Hana&rsquo;s semiconductor packaging work, in Thailand and China.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">IGBT and SiC power modules</span></div><div class="desc">Single- and multi-die module assembly, from bare die through to a tested module.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Intelligent power modules (IPM)</span></div><div class="desc">IPM assembly for motor-control designs, with the drive and power stages packaged together.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Substrate and thermal path</span></div><div class="desc">DBC ceramic substrate attach, high-thermal die attach, silver-sinter where specified, baseplate attach and controlled solder joints.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Heavy-current interconnect and encapsulation</span></div><div class="desc">Heavy copper (PCC) wire and clip bonding sized to the module&rsquo;s rated current, then encapsulation and finishing.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">See IC Assembly &amp; Test for the wider semiconductor packaging range this module work sits inside, from wafer processing through molding, plating and final test.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/osat">Explore IC Assembly &amp; Test <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--surface);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:720px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">The industrial duty cycle</h2><p class="mk-body" style="margin-top:14px;">A module going into a solar inverter or a variable-speed drive is switched for long stretches at whatever duty cycle its design sets, and it is the joints in the heat path &mdash; not the silicon &mdash; that the assembly has to get right. Voiding in the die-attach layer is controlled and verified, the attach material is matched to what the design specifies, and the substrate and baseplate joints are built to move heat out to the equipment&rsquo;s own cooling. Reliability and cycling test is available to the program&rsquo;s requirements, so a module can leave the line verified against its thermal design.</p><p class="mk-body" style="margin-top:14px;">Modules assembled here are specified into photovoltaic and wind converters, industrial inverters and motor drives, AC-DC and power-factor-correction stages, rail traction equipment and EV charging infrastructure. What the module has to achieve in each of those is set by the customer&rsquo;s design.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where it&#39;s made</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ayutthaya"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What industrial applications can Hana-assembled power modules serve?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Photovoltaic and wind converters, industrial inverters and motor drives, AC-DC and power-factor-correction stages, rail traction equipment and EV charging infrastructure. Hana assembles the module that goes into that equipment, not the finished equipment itself.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Can Hana assemble both IGBT and silicon-carbide modules?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Yes &mdash; IGBT and SiC die in single- and multi-die layouts, plus intelligent power modules (IPM) for motor control, with solder or silver-sinter die attach and heavy copper wire or clip interconnect.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How can an industrial power module be tested before it ships?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Reliability and cycling test can be set to the program&rsquo;s requirements, alongside the inspection applied through the build. What is applied to a given module is agreed during program review rather than fixed in advance.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How does this differ from the automotive and package-level power module pages?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">The device is the same; the framing differs. For in-vehicle powertrain programs see <a href="/markets/automotive/power-modules">Automotive power modules</a>; for package families and assembly discipline see <a href="/markets/power-management/igbt-sic-modules">IGBT &amp; SiC power modules</a>. This page covers industrial end uses.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/industrial-iot" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Industrial &amp; IoT market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your industrial power-module program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>

